# Citation File Format (CFF) 1.2.0 metadata for the corpus artifact
# accompanying the paper "LinguaGapAtlas" (earlier title: "Quantifying the Gaps").
# At release time: fill in the version actually released, its release date,
# and the DOI once one is minted (e.g. via the repository's archive release).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite the paper and this artifact."
title: "LinguaGapAtlas: A Corpus and Taxonomy of 96 Multilingual AI Benchmarks and Datasets"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Jajee
    given-names: Sankalp K.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8597-9042"
  - family-names: Shaw
    given-names: Tanisha
  - family-names: Soni
    given-names: Vatsalya
abstract: >-
  Structured corpus of 96 multilingual AI resources (65 benchmarks and 31
  datasets, 2018-2025) classified on five taxonomy dimensions - data origin,
  linguistic resource tier, task class, cultural specificity, and inference
  paradigm - with per-resource provenance, the 142-candidate screening log,
  the annotation codebook, and scripts that recompute the paper's headline
  statistics and inter-annotator agreement.
keywords:
  - multilingual AI
  - benchmarks
  - datasets
  - bias
  - evaluation
  - taxonomy
  - fairness
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.0.0
# date-released: YYYY-MM-DD   # set at release
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX  # set once minted; do not guess
